 The skills and instructions management catalog at `GET /sessions/{session_id}/catalog` is a fresh discovery view, separate from this prepared request snapshot. A candidate can appear there before a session reload makes it available at runtime; reloads can also update live commands while the cached system prompt remains pinned until compaction.
+
+## Request contribution inspection
+
+Saved request snapshots include typed `request_context` capture facts: opaque
+source IDs and diagnostics, included and omitted whole blocks, genuine capacity
+and provenance, initial static cost, final estimate and fit. Content pages use
+the exact assembled request's instructions/history/tools. Retry and inspection
+reuse the capture; a subsequent request captures the next live revision. The
+final estimator prices assembled content once, rather than adding its dynamic
+subtotal twice. Estimates are local byte-based approximations, not tokenizer
+guarantees. Unknown capacity stays unknown even for forced compaction.
+
+Preparation refusals save an explicitly failed capture inspection before pin
+settlement or compaction notifications. Successful earlier contributors survive
+a later callback/strategy failure. The generic refusal reason is capped at 2048
+Unicode scalars; source diagnostics retain the callback's bounded semantic
+contract. This failed attempt does not represent a sent provider request.
+
+The loop captures the accepted source query before image fitting appends
+request-only notes, carries it through tool continuations, and refreshes it from
+new steering. The preparation API receives that source query explicitly and
+enforces the same UTF-8 byte cap. It does not infer source actors from prose.
