 `notes` is a layer over whichever strategy is active, not a strategy: at every compaction the model rewrites its own notes, and they lead every later request. it is enabled by default and needs no strategy of its own. see [compaction](compaction.md).
 
 a `CleanPlugin` is how an extension that keeps rows per session deletes them with the session. every installed extension's runs inside the delete's transaction, enabled or not, before the session row goes, so an extension owns its tables and the daemon's delete lists only its own. the exception is `cells`, which the daemon deletes itself because it feeds the image reference count released in the same transaction.
+
+## Captured request context
+
+`RequestContextPlugin(prepare, required)` contributes bounded read-only native
+context once per actual request preparation. It receives the store/session, fully
+active bundle names, a recent user/steering query capped at 4096 UTF-8 bytes, and
+the genuine remaining window after static instructions and tool schemas. This is
+a trusted native semantic contract, not a security sandbox. The extension owns
+its coherent source revision and returns an opaque snapshot ID, whole mandatory
+or optional instruction/data blocks and diagnostics. Identity and memory policy
+do not belong to the host interface.
+
+The composition collects callbacks only from complete active bundles. A required
+requested bundle that failed loading refuses preparation. Any active callback
+error or exception stops preparation. Admission and capability inspection do not
+invoke callbacks. Dynamic data is never durable history or raw compaction input.
+
+Canonical required request declarations survive installation quarantine. Saved
+selection is checked before composing and on actual preparation, including a
+retained cached composition. Persisted session requirements additionally check
+complete active request-contributor owner names, so removing the entire owner
+cannot silently turn a required session into an ordinary session.
